Pseudo Classes: The Pseudo classes allow us to select the HTML elements based on their state like hover, visited etc. These states are not exact HTML elements, they
represent the current activity related to that element. The colon symbol (:) is used to select an HTML element based on its state.

Pseudo Elements: These are the elements which are not present in the HTML tree. They are created using CSS. It allow us to create HTML content without writing HTML.
The pseudo elements can be created using double column (::).
